# Cycle 1 
# Pull Request Review Process

**Status:** Accepted  
**Date:** 2026-09-29  
**Decision Owners:** Kadeeja Labaran, Team Lead

## Context

The team needed a consistent process for reviewing code before changes
are added to the main branch. 

The team wanted to reduce the risk of whats unreviewed.

## Decision

The team decided that every pull request must be reviewed and approved
by at least one team member (preferrably 2) before it can be merged.

## Alternatives Considered

### Alternative 1: Allow direct commits

We considered allowing members to commit changes directly without
requiring another team member to review them.

This was not selected because changes could be added without another
team member checking the work first.

## Consequences

### Positive

-Problems can be identified before changes reach the main branch.

### Negative / Trade-Offs

-Pull requests may take longer to merge while waiting for review.

## Evidence

- docs/planning/re-estimates

## Revisit Conditions

The team will reconsider this decision if the pull requests do not get approved in a reasonable time
